comments[31]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T15:48:14.615Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-09-01: history writes now carry public event_class=v1 classification; explicit classifications win, update patch fields are classified by declared policy, and unknown operations fail closed as substantive. The v3 event index supports latest-substantive reads with authoritative fallback. Context relevance and persisted signal snapshots derive recency from the latest substantive history event, then release cohort, then created_at, and never bare updated_at; explained context/next expose source, coordinate, history operation, and event class. A temporary-project acceptance proved a dependency-only maintenance write left the substantive recency coordinate byte-for-byte unchanged while CLI and PmClient returned the expected items. Static quality passed with public-surface and replication gates; exact coverage passed 596 files / 8260 tests at 60874 statements, 46011 branches, 12674 functions, and 58599 lines, all 100%. Supported Node 24 scale check remained within product bounds."
  "2026-09-01T17:16:28.944Z","harness:codex","Review round evidence: accepted findings added the real history:author-acknowledge, history_compact_baseline, and tests_remove maintenance operations; invalid persisted event_class values now fall through to the versioned classifier; history index v4 records authoritative stream byte sizes and rejects stale-but-valid projections before rebuilding; latest-event maps use null prototypes; signal snapshot v3 fingerprints exact recency evidence; DatabaseSync replication detects declarations and assignments. Non-absence I/O errors remain authoritative failures. Linked focused suite passed 49/49 and repo coverage passed 60,928/60,928 statements, 46,039/46,039 branches, 12,685/12,685 functions, 58,650/58,650 lines."
  "2026-09-01T18:28:29.526Z","harness:codex","Late-review hardening evidence: context snapshot freshness now fingerprints every item's effective recency provenance, including release-cohort and created_at fallbacks; optional substantive-history fields are isolated in their negative control. History-index rebuilds persist byte sizes captured with the authoritative pre-read snapshot, so a concurrent append leaves a detectable conservative mismatch rather than certifying old rows against a new size. Focused context/history suites passed, including the concurrent-append regression."
  "2026-09-01T19:41:37.247Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit follow-up evidence: v4 documentation now matches the runtime index; ContextSignalSnapshotItem requires ContextSignalProvenance on the public surface; persisted recency rejects maintenance history as substantive and rejects history fields on release/created fallbacks. Cross-process compliant appends now hold SQLite BEGIN IMMEDIATE across authoritative append, row insertion, and byte-size capture; append failure preserves the prior index, while post-append projection failure preserves history and removes the derived index. Focused 165-test coverage passed; exact repo coverage is 60,949/60,949 statements, 46,049/46,049 branches, 12,688/12,688 functions, and 58,670/58,670 lines; full static, zero-clone, docstring, contract, SDK surface, and record-integrity gates passed."
  "2026-09-01T19:59:44.203Z","harness:codex","Terminal review-fix evidence: history append/index coordination now acquires a SQLite BEGIN IMMEDIATE write transaction with a 5-second busy timeout before the authoritative append, serializes concurrent writers through committed byte-size capture, refuses the append if the lock cannot be acquired, preserves the prior projection when the authoritative append fails, and removes only the derived index when post-append projection work fails. Context signal snapshots now require parser-aligned typed provenance and reject contradictory fallback/history provenance; docs identify the current v4 index. Negative controls cover lock refusal, append failure, post-append projection failure, concurrency ordering, and contradictory provenance. Final full coverage: statements 60953/60953, branches 46049/46049, functions 12688/12688, lines 58674/58674. Final pnpm quality:static passed."
  "2026-09-01T20:30:54.275Z","harness:codex","Verification note: the first post-hardening full coverage run passed all product and integration tests except one 120-second timeout in tests/unit/scripts/release/surface-replication-gate.spec.ts. The complete 18-test file then passed in isolation in 23.91 seconds, confirming suite contention rather than a deterministic surface-replication failure. Rerunning the full linked gate for a terminal exact-coverage receipt."
  "2026-09-01T20:39:25.383Z","harness:codex","Implementation note: the DatabaseSync seam trigger test now verifies the complete configured trigger vocabulary directly and performs one representative relevant repository scan instead of four redundant scans. The isolated 18-test suite passes in 17.57 seconds and retains both unrelated-line and relevant-line behavior assertions."
  "2026-09-01T20:47:40.599Z","harness:codex","Coverage note: the successful contention-hardened full suite reached 60,988/60,989 statements and exposed only the non-ENOENT directory-read failure branch in general indexed queries. Added a real ELOOP history-directory acceptance path; the focused 20-test event-index suite and TypeScript gates pass. Rerunning the PM-linked exact gate for the terminal receipt."
  "2026-09-01T21:04:50.681Z","harness:codex","Final gate note: snapshot row/fingerprint consistency is now enforced at the untrusted parse boundary, keeping readOrRebuild below the strict complexity ceiling. pnpm quality:static passed all lint, zero-duplication, build, contract, docstring, package, refusal, token, graph, and record-integrity gates. The Node 24 five-iteration 10,000-item scale benchmark passed both transports with the 1,000 ms p95 and 5,000-token product targets. Running the final PM-linked exact coverage receipt after this refactor."
  "2026-09-01T21:12:22.335Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: final PM-linked focused suite passed 57/57 and repo-wide exact coverage passed at 60,991/60,991 statements, 46,066/46,066 branches, 12,700/12,700 functions, and 58,707/58,707 lines. quality:static passed; the five-run Node 24 10,000-item dual-transport scale benchmark passed; isolated manual init/create/claim/comment/context acceptance rebuilt then reused a fresh derived-index signal snapshot with substantive comment_add provenance, context usage delivery, and history-event-index SQLite state. Temporary acceptance data was moved recoverably to the desktop Trash."
  "2026-09-01T21:41:04.253Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review implementation: unique history-index lock owners now release only their own current lock; a contended optional index lock no longer blocks authoritative history append; drift-cache invalidation runs after the authoritative append/index transaction; sparse snapshots fail closed while v3 substantive provenance without event_class remains compatible."
  "2026-09-01T21:52:02.969Z","harness:codex","Verification note: the first exact-head full coverage rerun exposed only five schema-command expectations that encoded the history lock owner literal. The implementation now preserves that public owner and stores release uniqueness in private lock token metadata; the complete 175-test focused plus schema regression suite passes."
  "2026-09-01T22:00:37.823Z","harness:codex","Scale-gate correction: the first tokenized release implementation used the stale-cleanup gate for every ordinary unlock and made the scale generator miss its 30-second contention ceiling. Normal release now performs the token ownership check directly; stale takeover remains separately serialized. The focused history/lock/scale suite passes 76/76 with scale-workspace at 1.24 seconds."
  "2026-09-01T22:27:17.431Z","harness:codex","Terminal exact-head evidence: repo-wide coverage passed at 58,723/58,723 lines, 61,007/61,007 statements, 12,699/12,699 functions, and 46,099/46,099 branches. pnpm quality:static passed the complete ESLint, zero-duplication, build, contracts, SDK/package parity, agent-token, graph-composition, and record-integrity chain. A fresh temporary Git workspace initialized, created an item, and returned it through pm context; the SDK acceptance finalized one receipt twice and persisted exactly one correlated delivery. The temporary workspace was moved to Trash. Review hardening now uses private lock tokens so stale release closures cannot remove replacement locks, preserves authoritative history append when the optional derived-index lock is contended, invalidates drift state only after the authoritative append path completes, accepts valid legacy v3 provenance without event_class, and fails closed on sparse snapshots."
  "2026-09-01T23:05:05.084Z","harness:codex","Final review verification: the 118-test focused suite passed, including the deterministic locked-writer/unlocked-fallback race. Repo-wide exact coverage passed at 100/100/100/100. The first linked quality:static attempt reached repository assurance and failed only because pm-07pt16 and pm-wv47pf were deliberately non-terminal during review work; the defect-evidence gate correctly reported governed terminal defects=0. Closing the reviewed defects now and rerunning the same linked static command."
  "2026-09-01T23:17:48.041Z","harness:codex","Paired seam evidence: item-metadata index updates now resolve optional DatabaseSync availability before filesystem access; the paired 23-test query-index and replication suite passed, the live replication gate reports both members changed with density 1, and the final exact coverage rerun passed 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-09-01T23:47:43.784Z","harness:codex","Fresh-review correction evidence: restored sourceCursor=cursor-2 in the changedEvidence case so the persisted and requested cursors remain identical and only recency-evidence fingerprint drift can cause invalidation. The exact declared five-file linked suite, including surface-replication-gate.spec.ts, now has a matching canonical passing run: 5 files and 118 tests passed. Closure wording is restored to make substantive-history recency, maintenance invariance, explainable provenance, and concurrent derived-index safety the primary delivery; DatabaseSync replication alignment remains a supporting hardening detail."
  "2026-09-02T00:10:59.515Z","harness:codex","Exact-head implementation: indexed latest-substantive reads now distinguish lock contention from ordinary cache misses and fall straight back to authoritative streams after one lock budget instead of attempting a second contended rebuild. Blank public HistoryEntry timestamps are generated once before the paired file/index append, preventing ordering and filter divergence. Persisted recency provenance now requires a real string source before allowlist validation. The canonical five-file linked suite passes 120/120 with new timing, timestamp-equality, and array-source negative controls."
  "2026-09-02T00:17:39.168Z","harness:codex","Post-implementation-commit coverage evidence: after commit 7d7d5fe24, the canonical linked coverage command passed in 357.204s at exactly 61,013/61,013 statements, 46,117/46,117 branches, 12,701/12,701 functions, and 58,731/58,731 lines. This receipt unambiguously postdates the implementation commit; later PM-only closeout mutations do not change the tested source tree."
  "2026-09-02T00:25:02.018Z","harness:codex","Terminal static evidence: pnpm quality:static passed against implementation commit 7d7d5fe24 with both defect owners closed. ESLint, both zero-clone jscpd scans, build/contracts, repository assurance, SDK/package parity, replication/grammar/refusal/token gates, MCP deprecation inventory, tracker graph composition, and record integrity all passed."
