  "2026-09-02T01:20:58.127Z","harness:codex","Investigation note: exact-head review identified possible post-append projection invalidation rejection, a release/replacement race, insufficient recency-coordinate validation, a stale v3 doc reference, and an item-local coverage receipt gap. Verifying each against full source before edits."
  "2026-09-02T01:47:31.209Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review correction evidence: authoritative history appends now return success even when best-effort projection deletion fails, while retained projections fail byte-size validation; lock release and stale takeover share one cross-process mutation gate through ownership re-read and unlink; recency coordinates are RFC 3339-validated and UTC-canonicalized at build and parse boundaries; performance docs name index v4. Negative controls cover removal denial, release/replacement interleaving, and busy release gates. The item-owned focused suite passed 113/113, the item-owned repository gate passed 8,263 tests at exact 61,032/61,032 statements, 46,129/46,129 branches, 12,705/12,705 functions, and 58,748/58,748 lines, and the Node 24 five-run 10,000-item CLI/SDK scale contract passed both product ceilings."
  "2026-09-02T02:02:33.189Z","harness:codex","Final exact-head static evidence: CI=1 PM_NON_INTERACTIVE=1 pnpm quality:static passed the complete repository chain after the review fixes, including ESLint, both zero-clone jscpd scans, build and generated-contract checks, repository-static-quality, package boundary and SDK parity, CLI/MCP surface and grammar gates, refusal closure, deterministic 21-step agent-task token replay, MCP deprecation inventory, tracker-context-quality, gate registry, public SDK surface, SDK entrypoint and CLI transport costs, graph-composition, and record-integrity."
  "2026-09-02T02:38:56.609Z","harness:codex","Exact-head Cubic correction evidence: owned lock release now retries a transient cleanup gate and exits safely on replacement or bounded timeout; recency coordinates accept unambiguous date-only legacy values but reject invalid calendars and sub-millisecond precision that cannot round-trip; parser and projection-removal negative controls now prove their named boundary directly. The focused regression set passed 89/89, then the final repository gate passed all 8,285 tests at exact 61,049/61,049 statements, 46,140/46,140 branches, 12,705/12,705 functions, and 58,763/58,763 lines."
  "2026-09-02T03:12:23.652Z","harness:codex","Investigation note: exact-head CodeRabbit identified a durable projection-invalidation race, stale-cleanup gate ownership hazards, history timestamp validation gaps, build/parse provenance asymmetry, scale-target qualification, DatabaseSync return-path replication coverage, and weak negative controls. Verifying each against full source before edits."
  "2026-09-02T04:29:53.932Z","harness:codex","Exact-head terminal evidence: CodeRabbit review corrections now use a two-phase pending/committed invalidation protocol held under a dedicated lock across history append and index query/rebuild boundaries; malformed or submillisecond timestamps fail closed with history_timestamp_invalid; signal builders enforce parser-equivalent provenance; live cleanup-gate owners never age out; and only explicitly approved benchmark tiers enforce product targets. CI=1 PM_NON_INTERACTIVE=1 pnpm quality:static passed the complete static, SDK surface, graph, and record-integrity chain. The item-owned five-contract run passed, including the new 161-test review regression set and all 8,289 repository tests at exact 61,126/61,126 statements, 46,192/46,192 branches, 12,722/12,722 functions, and 58,837/58,837 lines. An isolated temporary-directory CLI acceptance initialized a project, created and commented pm-w3wj, retrieved it through context, closed it with structured evidence, and reread terminal state successfully."
  "2026-09-02T05:26:34.114Z","harness:codex","Exact-head Cubic correction evidence: strict history serialization now propagates timestamp validation errors for JSON-string overrides and rejects whitespace around authoritative timestamps; the v5 derived event index canonicalizes valid RFC3339 offsets to UTC for ordering and filters while preserving authoritative history bytes; context snapshots reject unsupported recency sources; stale-cleanup gates bind owners to Linux process-start identity with a bounded legacy fallback so PID reuse cannot preserve abandoned coordination forever; and scale tiers opt into one canonical product target instead of duplicating mutable thresholds. The focused 116-test regression set passed. The final repo-wide run passed all 8,293 tests at exactly 61,147/61,147 statements, 46,218/46,218 branches, 12,726/12,726 functions, and 58,856/58,856 lines; quality:static also passed before the two coverage-only negative controls were added."
  "2026-09-02T05:33:30.481Z","harness:codex","Terminal linked-test evidence: all five registered acceptance contracts passed after the Cubic corrections. The final focused matrix covered 165 tests; the canonical repo-wide linked run passed all 8,293 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, and every execution used the trusted local source branch with isolated PM schema state."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T15:48:17.264Z","harness:codex","Freshness is semantic event provenance, not file-write time: maintenance operations must be explicitly classified and excluded from temporal ranking, while unknown operations fail closed as substantive."
  "2026-09-01T19:41:37.711Z","harness:codex","A derived index can safely coordinate an authoritative append without a second filesystem lock by holding its SQLite write transaction across the append and paired size capture; if projection work fails after the append, preserve authority and discard the accelerator."
  "2026-09-01T20:11:24.024Z","harness:codex","SQLite row transactions alone do not coordinate a replace-by-rename rebuild or a stat-then-query read. A derived index that must be linearizable with compliant authoritative appends needs one shared cross-process coordination boundary spanning rebuild, append, validation, and read; the SQLite transaction remains the inner atomic projection commit."
